  "name": "coordination/dispatch-reply",
  "description": "`dispatch` on the coordination surface: the operator's one-shot consent receipt is spent and the dispatch is committed in one store transaction (ADR-0016 §2), and the staged bytes are then carried to the pinned recipient in a coordination envelope. `consent_spent` is always true on a successful reply and `replayed` distinguishes a fresh commit from an execution-key retry. `egress` reports where the bytes got to, read off a durable column rather than inferred: `sent` means the pinned recipient acknowledged this exact staged digest, `pending` means the dispatch committed and this endpoint has no such acknowledgement (what a crash between commit and send leaves), and `failed` means carriage was attempted and refused. `at` and `detail` are instance values; the frozen facts are the field sets and the state vocabulary.",
